348	// ── Fire-and-forget wrappers ──────────────────────────────────────────────
349	//
350	// These are the ones to call from request paths. They return void, never a
351	// promise, so there is no await to forget and no rejection to handle: a
352	// notification physically cannot delay or fail the request that triggered it.
353	//
354	// Nothing calls them yet — the routes that would (signup, generate, publish)
355	// are owned by other modules and this module may not edit them. Each is a
356	// single line at the call site:
